# Pin line endings so a Windows clone with stock Git-for-Windows settings
# (core.autocrlf=true) cannot corrupt the tree on its first commit. Without this,
# the repo is protected only by each contributor's local git config.
#
# Verified 2026-09-03 before adding: the repo is all-LF (1558 text files LF, 0
# CRLF/mixed) and has NO CRLF-mandatory files (.bat/.cmd/.sln), so eol=lf is safe
# and causes zero renormalization of existing files. `text=auto` leaves the ~50
# binary files (images, installer artifacts) untouched by auto-detecting them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF to run at all; state it explicitly so the intent is
# obvious and survives any future narrowing of the wildcard above.
*.sh text eol=lf
